; The `lowering-*` family had 29 cases and none for its central failure
; mode: a hook that refuses. Every other case in the family covers what the
; pass does when lowering *works* (or when the schema declaring it is
; wrong); this one covers the runtime saying no.
;
; `test/probe-wrong-call-v1` reads `:n` — declared `:type number` — through
; `input.symbol`, so the typed-read helper rejects the call and the hook
; returns `error.HookFailed`. Which refusal it is does not matter here; what
; matters is what the driver does with one. A hook failure is a *diagnostic*
; against the author's document: exactly one, at the source form, and the
; invocation is dropped so nothing partially-lowered reaches validation.
; Nothing crashes, and nothing is silently skipped.
;
; The corpus compares code, severity and path — not messages — so this case
; cannot pin the hook-supplied explanation that `LoweringOutput.fail` added.
; It pins the frame that carries it.
;
; Zig-runner-only, like every `lowering-*` case: the Web and Rust hosts
; drive `sjon.wasm`, which has no Zig-side hook registry.
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name sugar :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/probe-wrong-call-v1 :produces [target])
    (key :name n :type number))
  (form :name target :open true))

(sugar :n 1)
